realtime_tools: QNX support in realtime_helpers

realtime_helpers.cpp treats every Unix but macOS as Linux: it includes
<sys/capability.h> and links libcap (Linux capabilities, which QNX does not
have: "sys/capability.h: No such file or directory"), reads
/sys/kernel/realtime, and sets affinity with cpu_set_t and
pthread_setaffinity_np. On QNX:
- has_realtime_kernel(): true -- Neutrino is a real-time microkernel;
- configure_sched_fifo(): pthread_setschedparam() on the calling thread, as
  on macOS (QNX schedules threads; sched_setscheduler(0) would change the
  main thread's policy);
- lock_memory(): mlockall() alone (it needs PROCMGR_AID_MEM_LOCK, which
  root has), with strerror() for the reason it failed;
- set_thread_affinity(): the thread's runmask, ThreadCtlExt(_NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK)
  (a pthread_t is the thread ID).
No libcap on QNX.

Upstream-Status: Pending
